{"version":1,"content":"\n<p>尼泊爾排燈節（Tihar Festival，音譯提哈節，在印度則稱Diwali Festival）象徵光明驅走黑暗的傳統節日。在香港佐敦，尼泊爾裔社群熱鬧慶賀，為迎財富女神吉祥天女（Lakshmi），家家戶戶、地道商店與餐廳皆點亮了璀璨的燈飾與傳統油燈，街道上佈滿金黃色的萬壽菊花環，充滿濃厚的節慶氣氛。 <br/><br/>節慶期間，人們會進行莊嚴的祈福儀式迎吉祥天女（Lakshmi）。根據傳統習俗，信眾首先會在地上的彩繪圖騰旁點燃小油燈與蠟燭。他們會在祭盤中精心擺放香蕉等水果、傳統米漿圈（Sel Roti）以及各式祭品，再灑上萬壽菊花瓣，進行供奉，男女之間會互相在對方額頭點上象徵祝福的紅點（Tika），最後再雙手合十、互相躬身致意，展現彼此的敬重。<br/><br/>與達善節（Dashain）不同，達善節的提卡多由長輩向後輩點上，強調輩分與傳承；提哈節則更重視兄弟姊妹、男女之間的互相致意與祝福，尤其在最後一天的Bhai Tika，雙方互點提卡、交換花環與心意，強調平等與情誼。<br/><br/>2020年佐敦曾發生嚴重火警，一間尼泊爾餐廳在慶祝提哈節及生日派對期間，疑因油燈或蠟燭引燃隔音物料，釀成7人死亡、多人受傷的慘劇。 此次慘劇後，部分尼泊爾社區成員與商戶改用電子蠟燭代替傳統油燈，在保留點燈迎神的傳統之餘，也減少火險。今年佐敦的尼泊爾食肆與商店仍可見花環、供桌與燈火，社區以較安全的方式延續家鄉習俗。</p>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/20261114Tihar_Nepal-2000-x-1333-%E5%83%8F%E7%B4%A0-%E5%89%AF%E6%9C%AC-1-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/20261114Tihar_Nepal-2000-x-1333-%E5%83%8F%E7%B4%A0-%E5%89%AF%E6%9C%AC-2-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/20261114Tihar_Nepal-2000-x-1333-%E5%83%8F%E7%B4%A0-%E5%89%AF%E6%9C%AC-3-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/20261114Tihar_Nepal-2000-x-1333-%E5%83%8F%E7%B4%A0-%E5%89%AF%E6%9C%AC-4-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/20261114Tihar_Nepal-2000-x-1333-%E5%83%8F%E7%B4%A0-%E5%89%AF%E6%9C%AC-5-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/20261114Tihar_Nepal-2000-x-1333-%E5%83%8F%E7%B4%A0-%E5%89%AF%E6%9C%AC-6-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/20261114Tihar_Nepal-2000-x-1333-%E5%83%8F%E7%B4%A0-%E5%89%AF%E6%9C%AC-7-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/20261114Tihar_Nepal-2000-x-1333-%E5%83%8F%E7%B4%A0-%E5%89%AF%E6%9C%AC-8-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/20261114Tihar_Nepal-2000-x-1333-%E5%83%8F%E7%B4%A0-%E5%89%AF%E6%9C%AC-9-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"683\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/20261114Tihar_Nepal-2000-x-1333-%E5%83%8F%E7%B4%A0-%E5%89%AF%E6%9C%AC-10-1024x683.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n","scraped_at":"2026-11-14T18:29:02.146758+00:00","quality":{"score":2,"chars":584,"images":10,"source":"The Collective HK","fallback":"rss-http-error","origin":"wordpress-public-posts","completeness":"unverified"},"published_at":"2026-11-14T16:29:29+00:00","fetched_at":"2026-11-15T06:50:21.441442+00:00","content_updated_at":"2026-11-14T18:22:16.597781+00:00","content_hash":"e90d5055fc299c51635fecf746bd87a756a8056c4c70d443083a617b35a5cd5e","evidence_status":"partial","scrape_error":"HTTP 520","content_retention":null,"content_capture":null}